<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tulln</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tulln an der Donau</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tulln is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-austria">Lower Austria</a>, on the site of the Roman fort of Comagena. It was a residence of the Babenberg margraves before they moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/klosterneuburg">Klosterneuburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a>, and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nibelungenlied">Nibelungenlied</a> it is the place where Kriemhild meets Etzel. The painter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egon-schiele">Egon Schiele</a> was born there in 1890.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tulln.jpg" alt="Tulln" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GuentherZ · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GuentherZ_2010-04-24_0034_Tulln_Hauptplatz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
